On Fri, Dec 21, 2001 at 03:19:55PM +0100, Srebrenko Sehic wrote:

> When the machine power ups, no SRM console is presented, and only a
> 'blue screen' is shown. Is there any way I can get the SRM console or

Probably the NT loader (forgot the name).

> is the firmware hosed forever? Flashing it would probably help,
> however all instructions require a working SRM console.

Some alphas have a failsave jumper to force the rom to load the flash
rom from floppy. Images with SRM are available for these machines. After
loading from floppy, nothing is changed, you still have to enter the
command to flash the flashrom. So you can try this without "damaging"
the machine. I'm not sure which models support SRM and whether they have
the failsafe jumper.

Erik.

