> I don't know nothing about alpha, so the little SRM help was just
> great! I have installed from the snapshot version. I used a floppy to
> boot the installation. Since the Unix SRM didn't support the graphic
> card, I use a vt100 connected to serial1. The only problem I have is
> that the ethernet device, de0, doesn't
> work well: At boot it can't detect the cable and after few minutes
> it's comming alive.

Your ethernet throubles can be solved. The dc driver is much beter on a
DPW (at least at my DPW 500a).
Just do
# config -ef /bsd
disable de
quit
# reboot

de is preferred over dc, but in some case dc works beter than de.
This is described on
http://www.holland-consulting.net/tech/ocep/21143.html

Dries
