From openbsd-alpha  Thu Dec 06 20:15:09 2001
From: Dries Schellekens <gwyllion () ace ! ulyssis ! org>
Date: Thu, 06 Dec 2001 20:15:09 +0000
To: openbsd-alpha
Subject: Re: What is "unaligned access"
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=openbsd-alpha&m=100766975727634

Some information on the handling of unaligned access can be found in
/etc/sysctl.conf.

#machdep.unaligned_print=0      # 0 - disable printing of unaligned access
#machdep.unaligned_fix=0        # 0 - disable fixup of unaligned access
#machdep.unaligned_sigbus=0     # 0 - don't sigbus on unaligned access

BTW these seem to be missing in sysctl(8).

Dries
